{
 "question": "Is the shadow caster a valid inward offset of the surface the camera sees?",
 "method": "Both tests run on the evaluated modifier result, island by island, because the characters are interpenetrating primitives welded into one mesh. Signed volume: a closed surface pushed past its own middle comes out inside out and its signed volume flips sign. Containment: every caster vertex must be inside its own island's shell, decided by counting surface crossings along a fixed ray; when it is outside, the distance to the surface is reported. A light direction is deliberately not supplied here, so what is measured is the geometry rule alone.",
